* SD-1-style overdrive (the Boss Super OverDrive kind), from a service-manual style drawing: an input buffer, a non-inverting op-amp gain stage with the clipping diodes in
* its feedback, a one-pole low pass, an active tone stage, the LEVEL pot and the output buffer. Single 9 V supply, everything biased at 4.5 V (VB).
*
* Gain stage (U1, 4558 type): input C2 .018 into R4 100k; the inverting leg is R6 4.7k with C3 .047 (a highpass near 720 Hz), the feedback is R5 33k plus the 1M DRIVE pot
* (VRD, used as a variable resistor) with the diodes across it: one diode (D4) for the output going down and two in series (D5, D6) for the output going up, so the clipping is
* asymmetrical (the single diode clips first). Behind it R7 10k with C4 .018 (a low pass near 880 Hz).
* Tone (U2): the low pass feeds its + input; the TONE pot VR3 (20k) joins that node (VRT_A), the wiper (to ground through C5 .027 and R8 470) and the - input (VRT_B), and the feedback is
* R9 10k with C6 .01. LEVEL (VRL_T, VRL_B, 10k) follows C7 1u and R10 4.7k.
* The input and output transistors (Q5, Q6) are emitter followers: here ideal buffers, with the input loaded like the real base (R2 470k with an assumed 1M for the transistor's gain).
* Assumptions: the diodes are 1N4148-like (the drawing does not say which type); the op-amps are the limited element around the 4.5 V bias, 3.3 V soft limit on 9 V.

V VB vb 1 4.5
C CB vb 0 47u

I VIN gin 1
R R1 gin a 10k
C C1 a b 0.047u
R R2 b vb 470k
R RQ5 b vb 1M
O UQ5 b nq q vb RC4558
R RFQ5 q nq 1

* Gain stage.
C C2 q g 0.018u
R R4 g vb 100k
O U1 g inv o1 vb RC4558
R R6 inv i6 4.7k
C C3 i6 vb 0.047u
R R5 inv fb 33k
R VRD fb o1 1
D D4 inv o1 SIGNAL
D D6 o1 dd SIGNAL
D D5 dd inv SIGNAL

* Low pass and tone stage.
R R7 o1 t1 10k
C C4 t1 vb 0.018u
O U2 t1 inv2 o2 vb RC4558
R R9 inv2 o2 10k
C C6 inv2 o2 0.01u
R VRT_A t1 w3 1
R VRT_B w3 inv2 1
C C5 w3 c5 0.027u
R R8 c5 vb 470

* Level and the output buffer.
C C7 o2 c7 1u
R R10 c7 l3 4.7k
R VRL_T l3 y 1
R VRL_B y 0 1
R R17 y 0 1M
